<title>NETHERLANDS: SOCCER-VALCKX RETIRES FROM INTERNATIONALS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-VALCKX RETIRES FROM INTERNATIONALS.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch defender Stan Valckx retired from international soccer ahead of Saturday's World Cup qualifier against San Marino, Dutch news agency ANP said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Valckx, 33, said he could not physically continue to play in both the national side and PSV Eindhoven. He played 20 times for the Netherlands.</p>
<p>Dutch coach Guus Hiddink did not immediately call in a replacement.</p>
<p>The Netherlands play San Marino in Amsterdam on Saturday and meet Turkey away next Wednesday in another World Cup group seven qualifier.</p>
